+/* The Master Collection intercepts KEY CONFIG. It replaces the six instructions
+   that begin `case 8`'s third branch below (retail 0x800C550C, the first KEY
+   CONFIG cursor call) with
+
+       lui   v1, 0x8020        ; 0x80200000 - the emulator's doorbell, the one
+       lui   v0, 0x0000        ; address MGSM2Fix's Ketchup deliberately never
+       addiu v0, v0, 1         ; blocks, even with DisableRAM on
+       sw    v0, 0(v1)
+       j     0x800C5684        ; option_800C5150's epilogue, 20 bytes before
+       nop                     ; the next function
+
+   so selecting KEY CONFIG rings the doorbell and returns WITHOUT transitioning
+   to state 9. Its own Control Settings panel then draws over the OPTION menu -
+   which is why its screen still shows the OPTION rows behind it.
+
+   That patch is `disc1_16F8E024_patch.bin`, keyed to a byte offset inside
+   retail's overlay. This overlay is recompiled and 172 bytes shorter, and the
+   English port relocates the whole option stage into DUMMY3M besides, so the
+   patch lands on bytes the game never reads and the interception was lost.
+   Hence reproducing it here rather than inheriting it: ours works wherever the
+   stage ends up living.
+
+   Set to 0 for a raw PSX disc, where there is no collection to intercept
+   anything, 0x80200000 is past the end of a retail console's 2 MB, and the
+   ported KEY CONFIG screen is the entire point of porting its text. */
